; equality_length_mismatch_beats_model_type: the vecs are compared before
; the model register is discriminated.
;
; exec_equality resolves both vec operands, compares their lengths, and only
; then charges and reaches `as_model_mut()`. xqvm_py resolved the model
; register first, so an int in r0 answered TypeMismatch here and
; VecLengthMismatch there -- one program with two fault identities, which
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md's Faults table makes a divergence rather than a
; formatting difference.
;
; r0 deliberately holds an int rather than a sample: a sample would put the
; disagreement inside SPEC.md's XqmxMode carve-out and prove nothing about
; the ordering. An int is outside it, so this vector pins the rule.

PUSH 0
STOW r0          ; r0 is an int, not a model

VEC r2
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r2       ; indices has 1 entry

VEC r3           ; coeffs has 0

PUSH 0           ; target
PUSH 1           ; penalty
EQUALITY r0 r2 r3
HALT
